1
00:00:01,529 --> 00:00:09,529
Chapter 5 5 o'clock had hardly struck on the morning of the 19th of January,

2
00:00:10,369 --> 00:00:16,150
when Bessie brought a candle into my closet and found me already up and nearly dressed.

3
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:22,430
I had risen half an hour before her entrance and had washed my face and put on

4
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:26,046
my clothes by the light of a half moon, just setting,

5
00:00:26,047 --> 00:00:29,529
whose rays streamed through the narrow window near my crib.

6
00:00:31,255 --> 00:00:35,561
I was to leave Gateshead that day by a coach, which passed the

7
00:00:35,563 --> 00:00:41,310
lodge gates at 6 a .m., Bessie was the only person yet risen.

8
00:00:42,279 --> 00:00:47,810
She had lit a fire in the nursery, where she now proceeded to make my breakfast.

9
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:53,310
Few children can eat when excited with the thoughts of a journey, nor could I.

10
00:00:54,414 --> 00:00:59,170
Bessie, having pressed me in vain to take a few spoonfuls of the boiled milk and

11
00:00:59,171 --> 00:01:02,180
bread she had prepared for me, wrapped up some

12
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:04,869
biscuits in a paper and put them into my bag.

13
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:11,890
Then she helped me on with my police and bonnet, and wrapping herself in a shawl,

14
00:01:12,689 --> 00:01:14,630
she and I left the nursery.

15
00:01:16,324 --> 00:01:22,529
As we passed Mrs. Reed's bedroom, she said, Will you go in and bid Mrs.

16
00:01:22,689 --> 00:01:23,689
Goodbye?

17
00:01:24,289 --> 00:01:29,489
No, Bessie, she came to my crib last night when you were gone down to supper and said

18
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:33,630
I need not disturb her in the morning, all my cousins either.

19
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:38,579
And she told me to remember that she had always been my best

20
00:01:38,581 --> 00:01:42,350
friend and to speak of her and be grateful to her accordingly.

21
00:01:43,789 --> 00:01:44,829
What did you say, Miss?

22
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:47,210
Nothing.

23
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:51,609
I covered my face with the bedclothes and turned from her to the wall.

24
00:01:53,039 --> 00:01:54,350
That was wrong, Miss Jane.

25
00:01:55,229 --> 00:01:56,590
It was quite right Bessie.

26
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,390
Your Mrs. has not been my friend.

27
00:02:00,029 --> 00:02:01,649
She has been my foe.

28
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:04,010
Oh, Miss Jane, don't say so.

29
00:02:05,189 --> 00:02:08,172
Goodbye to Gateshead, cried I, as we passed

30
00:02:08,173 --> 00:02:11,070
through the hall and went out at the front door.

31
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:15,189
The moon was set, and it was very dark.

32
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:19,529
Bessie carried a lantern whose light glanced on

33
00:02:19,529 --> 00:02:23,069
wet steps and gravel road sodden by a recent thaw.

34
00:02:24,170 --> 00:02:26,430
Raw and chill was the winter morning.

35
00:02:27,109 --> 00:02:30,149
My teeth chatted as I hastened down the drive.

36
00:02:31,659 --> 00:02:33,449
There was a light in the porter's lodge.

37
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:38,489
When we reached it, we found the porter's wife just kindling her fire.

38
00:02:39,449 --> 00:02:44,810
My trunk, which had been carried down the evening before, stood corded at the door.

39
00:02:46,039 --> 00:02:50,590
It wanted but a few minutes of six, and shortly after that hour had struck,

40
00:02:51,199 --> 00:02:54,369
the distant roll of wheels announced the coming coach.

41
00:02:55,340 --> 00:03:00,250
I went to the door and watched its lamps approach rapidly through the gloom.

42
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:04,670
Is she going by herself, as the porter's wife?

43
00:03:05,289 --> 00:03:06,289
Yes.

44
00:03:06,489 --> 00:03:07,489
And how far is it?

45
00:03:08,149 --> 00:03:09,149
50 miles.

46
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:10,890
What a long way.

47
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,390
I wonder Mrs. Reed is not afraid to trust her so far alone.

48
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,630
The coach drew up.

49
00:03:17,149 --> 00:03:21,989
There it was at the gates with its four horses and its top laden with passengers.

50
00:03:23,109 --> 00:03:26,029
The guard and coachman loudly urged haste.

51
00:03:26,229 --> 00:03:27,529
My trunk was hoisted up.

52
00:03:28,359 --> 00:03:31,630
I was taken from Bessie's neck to which I clung with kisses.

53
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:36,185
Be sure and take good care of her, cried she

54
00:03:36,186 --> 00:03:39,091
to the guard, as he lifted me into the inside.

55
00:03:39,750 --> 00:03:40,930
I was the answer.

56
00:03:41,569 --> 00:03:46,409
The door was slapped to a voice exclaimed, all right, and on we drove.

57
00:03:47,510 --> 00:03:51,869
Thus was I severed from Bessie and Gateshead, thus world away to unknown,

58
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:56,829
and as I then deemed, remote and mysterious regions.

59
00:03:58,029 --> 00:03:59,789
I remember but little of the journey.

60
00:04:00,555 --> 00:04:04,314
I only know that the day seemed to me of a preternatural length,

61
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:08,329
and that we appeared to travel over hundreds of miles of road.

62
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:16,070
We passed through several towns, and in one, a very large one, the coach stopped.

63
00:04:16,529 --> 00:04:20,949
The horses were taken out, and the passengers are lighted to dine.

64
00:04:22,779 --> 00:04:26,569
I was carried into an inn where the guard wanted me to have some dinner.

65
00:04:27,649 --> 00:04:33,409
But, as I had no appetite, he left me in an immense room with a fireplace at each

66
00:04:33,411 --> 00:04:39,010
end, a chandelier pendant from the ceiling, and a little red gallery high up

67
00:04:39,011 --> 00:04:41,630
against the wall filled with musical instruments.

68
00:04:43,770 --> 00:04:49,390
Here I walked about for a long time, feeling very strange, and mortally

69
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:52,449
apprehensive of someone coming in and kidnapping me.

70
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:57,657
For, I believed in kidnappers, their exploits having

71
00:04:57,658 --> 00:05:01,149
frequently figured in Bessie's fireside chronicles.

72
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,970
At last the guard returned.

73
00:05:04,850 --> 00:05:07,430
Once more, I was stowed away in the coach.

74
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:11,930
My protector mounted his own seat, sounded his hollow

75
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:16,010
horn, and away we rattled over the stony street of L.

76
00:05:17,569 --> 00:05:20,189
The afternoon came on wet and somewhat misty.

77
00:05:21,470 --> 00:05:25,869
As it wamed into dusk, I began to feel that we were getting very far,

78
00:05:25,989 --> 00:05:27,010
indeed, from Gateshead.

79
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:30,029
We ceased to pass through towns.

80
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,130
The country changed.

81
00:05:32,829 --> 00:05:35,729
Great gray hills heaved up around the horizon.

82
00:05:36,819 --> 00:05:41,277
As twilight deepened, we descended a valley, dark with

83
00:05:41,278 --> 00:05:44,569
wood, and long after night had overclouded the prospect.

84
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:48,130
I heard a wild wind rushing amongst trees.

85
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:52,909
Lulled by the sound, I had last dropped a sleep.

86
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:57,590
I had not long slumbered when the sudden cessation of motion awoke me.

87
00:05:58,329 --> 00:06:02,890
The coach door was open, and a person like a servant was standing at it.

88
00:06:03,699 --> 00:06:06,409
I saw her face and dress by the light of the lamps.

89
00:06:07,859 --> 00:06:10,090
Is there a little girl called Jane Eyre here?

90
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:11,670
She asked.

91
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:15,550
I answered yes, and was then lifted out.

92
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:20,510
My trunk was handed down, and the coach instantly drove away.

93
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:27,631
I was stiff with long sitting, and bewildered with the noise and motion of the coach.

94
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:30,890
Gathering my faculties, I looked about me.

95
00:06:32,029 --> 00:06:34,810
Rain, wind, and darkness filled the air.

96
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:40,529
Nevertheless, I dimly discerned a wall before me, and a door opened in it.

97
00:06:41,409 --> 00:06:43,689
Through this door, I passed with my new guide.

98
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,329
She shut and locked it behind her.

99
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:52,250
There was now visible a house, or houses, for the building spread far,

100
00:06:52,970 --> 00:06:55,250
with many windows and lights burning in some.

101
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:02,490
We went up a broad pebbly path, splashing wet, and were admitted at a door.

102
00:07:03,069 --> 00:07:05,545
Then the servant led me through a passage into

103
00:07:05,546 --> 00:07:08,990
a room with a fire, where she left me alone.

104
00:07:10,270 --> 00:07:15,409
I stood and warmed my numbed fingers over the blaze, then I looked round.

105
00:07:16,430 --> 00:07:21,550
There was no candle, but the uncertain light from the hearth showed by intervals,

106
00:07:22,210 --> 00:07:27,010
papered walls, carpet, curtains, shining mahogany furniture.

107
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:32,609
It was a parlour, not so spacious or splendid as the drawing room at Gateshead,

108
00:07:33,170 --> 00:07:34,409
but comfortable enough.

109
00:07:36,579 --> 00:07:41,010
I was puzzling to make out the subject of a picture on the wall, when the door

110
00:07:41,011 --> 00:07:47,109
opened, and an individual carrying a light entered, another followed close behind.

111
00:07:48,029 --> 00:07:53,970
The first was a tall lady with dark hair, dark eyes, and a pale and large forehead.

112
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:59,189
Her figure was partly enveloped in a shawl, her countenance was grave,

113
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:00,789
her bearing erect.

114
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:05,234
The child is very young to be sent alone, said

115
00:08:05,234 --> 00:08:08,831
she, putting her candle down on the table.

116
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:13,649
She considered me attentively for a minute or two, then further added.

117
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:17,289
She had better be put to bed soon.

118
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:18,710
She looks tired.

119
00:08:20,175 --> 00:08:21,175
Are you tired?

120
00:08:21,609 --> 00:08:24,149
She asked, placing her hand on my shoulder.

121
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,270
A little man.

122
00:08:26,979 --> 00:08:31,449
And hungry too, no doubt, let her have some supper before she goes to bed,

123
00:08:31,609 --> 00:08:32,609
Miss Miller.

124
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:38,729
Is this the first time you have left your parents to come to school?

125
00:08:39,470 --> 00:08:40,390
My little girl?

126
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:43,649
I explained to her that I had no parents.

127
00:08:44,890 --> 00:08:50,909
She inquired how long they had been dead, then how old I was, what was my name,

128
00:08:51,569 --> 00:08:53,670
whether I could read, write, and so a little.

129
00:08:54,850 --> 00:09:01,550
Then she touched my cheek gently with her forefinger, and saying, she hoped I should

130
00:09:01,551 --> 00:09:04,829
be a good child, dismissed me along with Miss Miller.

131
00:09:05,930 --> 00:09:08,670
The lady I had left might be about 29.

132
00:09:09,810 --> 00:09:12,829
The one who went with me appeared some years younger.

133
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:17,250
The first impressed me by her voice, look, and air.

134
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:23,609
Miss Miller was more ordinary, ruddy in complexion, though of a care-worn

135
00:09:23,610 --> 00:09:27,172
countenance, hurried in gate and action, like one

136
00:09:27,173 --> 00:09:30,850
who had always a multiplicity of tasks on hand.

137
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:37,529
She looked, indeed, what I afterwards found she really was an underteacher.

138
00:09:38,850 --> 00:09:44,489
Led by her, I passed from compartment to compartment, from passage to passage,

139
00:09:45,539 --> 00:09:47,550
of a large and irregular building.

140
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:53,409
Till emerging from the total and somewhat dreary silence, pervading that portion of

141
00:09:53,411 --> 00:09:59,130
the house we had traversed, we came upon the hum of many voices, and presently

142
00:09:59,131 --> 00:10:05,270
entered a wide, long room, with great deal tables, two at each end, on each of which

143
00:10:05,369 --> 00:10:09,534
burned a pair of candles, and seated all round on benches, a

144
00:10:09,536 --> 00:10:15,229
congregation of girls of every age, from nine or ten to twenty.

145
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:21,789
Seen by the dim light of the dips, their number to me appeared countless,

146
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:24,909
though not in reality exceeding eighty.

147
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,788
They were uniformly dressed in brown stuff frocks

148
00:10:28,789 --> 00:10:32,190
of quaint fashion, and long Holland pinnifles.

149
00:10:32,930 --> 00:10:34,250
It was the hour of study.

150
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:40,189
They were engaged in conning over their tomorrow's task, and the harm I had heard

151
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:43,890
was the combined result of their whispered repetitions.

152
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:50,270
Miss Miller signed to me to sit on a bench near the door, then walking up to the top

153
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:56,890
of the long room, she cried out, monitors, collect the lesson books and put them away.

154
00:10:58,310 --> 00:11:01,753
Four tall girls arose from different tables, and

155
00:11:01,755 --> 00:11:04,810
going round gathered the books and removed them.

156
00:11:05,909 --> 00:11:11,610
Miss Miller again gave the word of command, monitors fetched the supper trays.

157
00:11:13,010 --> 00:11:17,569
The tall girls went out and returned presently, each bearing a tray,

158
00:11:18,289 --> 00:11:23,034
with portions of something I knew not what, arranged thereon,

159
00:11:23,036 --> 00:11:26,510
and a picture of water and mug in the middle of each tray.

160
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,390
The portions were handed around.

161
00:11:30,369 --> 00:11:34,810
Those who liked took a draft of the water, the mug being common to all.

162
00:11:35,939 --> 00:11:41,109
When it came to my turn, I drank, for I was thirsty, but did not touch the

163
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:45,109
food, excitement and fatigue rendering me incapable of eating.

164
00:11:46,329 --> 00:11:51,930
I now saw, however, that it was a thin, oat and cake shared into fragments.

165
00:11:52,869 --> 00:11:57,529
The meal over, prayers were read by Miss Miller, and the classes filed off,

166
00:11:58,010 --> 00:11:59,670
two and two upstairs.

167
00:12:01,529 --> 00:12:04,301
Overpowered by this time with weariness, I scarcely

168
00:12:04,301 --> 00:12:08,609
noticed what sort of a place the bedroom was, except that.

169
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:12,590
Like the schoolroom, I saw it was very long.

170
00:12:13,689 --> 00:12:16,449
Tonight, I was to be Miss Miller's bed -fellow.

171
00:12:17,369 --> 00:12:18,770
She helped me to undress.

172
00:12:20,109 --> 00:12:23,512
When laid down, I glanced at the long rows of beds,

173
00:12:23,514 --> 00:12:26,909
each of which was quickly filled with two occupants.

174
00:12:27,729 --> 00:12:31,171
In ten minutes, the single light was extinguished, and

175
00:12:31,171 --> 00:12:35,229
amidst silence and complete darkness, I fell asleep.

176
00:12:36,770 --> 00:12:38,569
The night passed rapidly.

177
00:12:39,619 --> 00:12:41,489
I was too tired even to dream.

178
00:12:42,649 --> 00:12:48,750
I only once awoke to hear the wind rave in furious gusts, and the rain fall in

179
00:12:48,751 --> 00:12:53,409
torrents, and to be sensible that Miss Miller had taken her place by my side.

180
00:12:54,430 --> 00:12:58,189
When I again unclosed my eyes, a loud bell was ringing.

181
00:12:59,289 --> 00:13:00,550
The girls were up and dressing.

182
00:13:01,529 --> 00:13:07,070
Day had not yet begun to dawn, and a rush-light or two burned in the room.

183
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:09,050
I too rose reluctantly.

184
00:13:09,829 --> 00:13:15,510
It was bitter cold, and I dressed as well as I could for shivering, and washed when

185
00:13:15,511 --> 00:13:20,909
there was a basin at liberty, which did not occur soon, as there was but one basin

186
00:13:20,911 --> 00:13:24,270
to six girls on the stands down the middle of the room.

187
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:30,569
Again, the bell rang, all formed in file, two and two.

188
00:13:31,609 --> 00:13:37,530
And in that order descended the stairs, and entered the cold and dimly lit schoolroom.

189
00:13:38,029 --> 00:13:40,229
Here, prayers were read by Miss Miller.

190
00:13:41,210 --> 00:13:47,130
Afterwards, she called out, form classes, a great tumult succeeded for some minutes,

191
00:13:47,789 --> 00:13:52,130
during which Miss Miller repeatedly exclaimed, silence and order.

192
00:13:53,529 --> 00:13:57,949
When it subsided, I saw them all drawn up in four semi-circles.

193
00:13:58,609 --> 00:14:03,949
Before four chairs placed at the four tables, all held books in their hands,

194
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:09,409
and a great book like a Bible lay on each table before the vacant seat.

195
00:14:10,789 --> 00:14:16,829
A pause of some seconds succeeded, filled up by the low vague hum of numbers,

196
00:14:17,710 --> 00:14:22,729
Miss Miller walked from class to class, hushing this indefinite sound.

197
00:14:23,350 --> 00:14:27,652
A distant bell tinkled, immediately three ladies entered

198
00:14:27,653 --> 00:14:30,529
the room, each walked to a table and took her seat.

199
00:14:31,609 --> 00:14:35,550
Miss Miller assumed the fourth vacant chair, which was that nearest the door,

200
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:40,329
and around which the smallest of the children were assembled, to this inferior

201
00:14:40,331 --> 00:14:43,810
class I was called, and placed at the bottom of it.

202
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:46,310
Business now began.

203
00:14:47,210 --> 00:14:52,010
The days collect was repeated, then certain texts of scripture were said,

204
00:14:52,710 --> 00:14:55,413
and to these succeeded a protracted reading

205
00:14:55,414 --> 00:14:58,630
of chapters in the Bible which lasted an hour.

206
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:04,850
By the time that exercise was terminated, day had fully dawned.

207
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:09,729
The indefatigable bell now sounded for the fourth time.

208
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:14,229
The classes were marshalled and marched into another room to breakfast.

209
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:19,170
How glad I was to behold a prospect of getting something to eat.

210
00:15:19,909 --> 00:15:24,909
I was now nearly sick from inenition, having taken so little the day before.

211
00:15:26,199 --> 00:15:32,510
The refactory was a great, low-sealed, gloomy room, on two long tables smoked

212
00:15:32,511 --> 00:15:36,423
basins of something hot, which, however, to my

213
00:15:36,425 --> 00:15:39,649
dismay, sent forth an odour far from inviting.

214
00:15:41,010 --> 00:15:46,050
I saw a universal manifestation of discontent when the fumes of the repast

215
00:15:46,449 --> 00:15:49,329
met the nostrils of those destined to swallow it.

216
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:53,309
From the van of the procession, the tall girls

217
00:15:53,310 --> 00:15:56,150
of the first class rose the whispered words.

218
00:15:57,069 --> 00:15:58,069
Disgusting!

219
00:15:58,510 --> 00:15:59,810
The porridge is burnt again.

220
00:16:01,409 --> 00:16:04,109
Silence, ejaculated a voice.

221
00:16:04,859 --> 00:16:09,649
Not that of Smiller, but one of the upper teachers, a little and dark personage,

222
00:16:10,130 --> 00:16:15,550
smartly dressed, but of somewhat morose aspect, who installed herself at the top

223
00:16:15,551 --> 00:16:20,090
of one table, while a more buxum lady presided at the other.

224
00:16:21,395 --> 00:16:24,890
I looked in vain for her I had first seen the night before.

225
00:16:25,829 --> 00:16:27,109
She was not visible.

226
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:32,217
Miss Miller occupied the foot of the table where I

227
00:16:32,219 --> 00:16:36,449
sat, and a strange, foreign -looking, elderly lady.

228
00:16:37,229 --> 00:16:39,725
The French teacher, as I afterwards found,

229
00:16:39,725 --> 00:16:43,591
took the corresponding seat at the other board.

230
00:16:43,930 --> 00:16:46,369
A long grace was said, and a hymn sung.

231
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:51,470
Then a servant brought in some tea for the teachers, and the meal began.

232
00:16:52,729 --> 00:16:58,529
Ravenous, and now very faint, I devoured a spoonful or two of my portion without

233
00:16:58,530 --> 00:17:02,989
thinking of its taste, but the first edge of hunger blunted.

234
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:07,029
I perceived I had got in hand a nauseous mess.

235
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:11,130
Burnt porridge is almost as bad as rotten potatoes.

236
00:17:12,409 --> 00:17:14,810
Famine itself soon sikens over it.

237
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,449
The spoons were moved slowly.

238
00:17:18,590 --> 00:17:21,699
I saw each girl taste her food and try to swallow it,

239
00:17:21,701 --> 00:17:24,770
but in most cases the effort was soon relinquished.

240
00:17:25,470 --> 00:17:28,449
Breakfast was over, and none had breakfasted.

241
00:17:29,539 --> 00:17:34,029
Thanks being returned for what we had not got, and a second hymn chanted,

242
00:17:34,710 --> 00:17:37,130
the Refectory was evacuated for the schoolroom.

243
00:17:37,989 --> 00:17:43,590
I was one of the last to go out, and in passing the tables, I saw one

244
00:17:43,591 --> 00:17:46,630
teacher, take a basin of the porridge and taste it.

245
00:17:47,289 --> 00:17:51,510
She looked at the others, all their countenances expressed displeasure,

246
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:55,970
and one of them, the stout one, whispered, abominable stuff.

247
00:17:56,949 --> 00:17:57,949
How shameful.

248
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:05,529
A quarter of an hour passed, before lessons again began, during which the

249
00:18:05,530 --> 00:18:10,350
schoolroom was in a glorious tumult, for that space of time it seemed to be

250
00:18:10,350 --> 00:18:14,850
permitted to talk loud and more freely, and they used their privilege.

251
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:22,091
The whole conversation ran on the breakfast, which one and all abused roundly.

252
00:18:22,664 --> 00:18:23,670
Poor things.

253
00:18:24,489 --> 00:18:26,890
It was the sole consolation they had.

254
00:18:27,930 --> 00:18:30,869
Miss Miller was now the only teacher in the room.

255
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:36,550
A group of great girls standing about her spoke with serious and sullen gestures.

256
00:18:37,619 --> 00:18:43,970
I heard the name of Mr. Brockelhurst, pronounced by some lips, at which Miss

257
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:47,431
Miller shook her head disapprovingly, but she made no great

258
00:18:47,432 --> 00:18:52,569
effort to check the general wrath, doubtless she shared in it.

259
00:18:53,609 --> 00:18:55,710
A clock in the schoolroom struck nine.

260
00:18:56,630 --> 00:18:58,356
Miss Miller left her circle and standing in the

261
00:18:58,457 --> 00:19:03,270
middle of the room cried, silence to your seats.

262
00:19:05,090 --> 00:19:06,409
Discipline prevailed.

263
00:19:07,449 --> 00:19:12,529
In five minutes the confused throng was resolved into order and comparative

264
00:19:12,530 --> 00:19:15,369
silence quelled the babble clamor of tongues.

265
00:19:16,479 --> 00:19:23,170
The upper teachers now punctually resumed their posts, but still all seemed to wait.

266
00:19:24,289 --> 00:19:30,770
Ranged on benches down the sides of the room, the 80 girls sat motionless and erect.

267
00:19:31,109 --> 00:19:34,506
A quaint assemblage they appeared, all with plain

268
00:19:34,507 --> 00:19:38,529
locks combed from their faces, not a curl visible.

269
00:19:39,229 --> 00:19:44,449
In brown dresses, made high and surrounded by a narrow tucker about the throat,

270
00:19:45,079 --> 00:19:49,489
with little pockets of Holland, shaped something like a highlander's

271
00:19:49,490 --> 00:19:55,791
purse, tied in front of their frocks, and destined to serve the purpose of a workbag.

272
00:19:56,465 --> 00:19:59,097
All too, wearing woolen stockings and

273
00:19:59,099 --> 00:20:03,190
country-made shoes, fastened with brass buckles.

274
00:20:03,989 --> 00:20:08,970
Above 20 of those clad in this costume were full grown girls, or rather young

275
00:20:08,970 --> 00:20:14,329
women, it suited them ill, and gave an air of oddity even to the prettiest.

276
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:19,869
I was still looking at them, and also at intervals examining the teachers,

277
00:20:20,649 --> 00:20:22,529
none of whom precisely pleased me.

278
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:28,170
For the stout one was a little course, the dark one, not a little fierce,

279
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:33,418
the foreigner, harsh and grotesque, and Miss Miller, poor

280
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:37,430
thing, looked purple, weather-beaten, and overworked.

281
00:20:37,909 --> 00:20:42,869
When, as my eye wandered from face to face, the whole school rose

282
00:20:42,871 --> 00:20:46,189
simultaneously, as if moved by a common spring.

283
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:48,350
What was the matter?

284
00:20:49,010 --> 00:20:50,569
I had heard no order given.

285
00:20:51,350 --> 00:20:52,350
I was puzzled.

286
00:20:53,329 --> 00:20:58,090
Air I had gathered my wits, the classes were again seated, but as all eyes were

287
00:20:58,091 --> 00:21:02,684
now turned to one point, mine followed the general direction,

288
00:21:02,685 --> 00:21:07,430
and encountered the personage who had received me last night.

289
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:11,569
She stood at the bottom of the long room on the half.

290
00:21:12,529 --> 00:21:15,489
For there was a fire at each end, she surveyed

291
00:21:15,490 --> 00:21:19,810
the two rows of girls silently and gravely.

292
00:21:20,649 --> 00:21:25,640
Miss Miller approaching seemed to ask her a question, and having received her

293
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:29,510
answer, went back to her place, and said aloud,

294
00:21:29,511 --> 00:21:32,760
monitor of the first class, fetch the globes.

295
00:21:34,510 --> 00:21:40,621
While the direction was being executed, the lady consulted, moved slowly up the room.

296
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:46,720
I suppose I have a considerable organ of veneration, for I retain yet the sense of

297
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,420
admiring awe, with which my eyes traced her steps.

298
00:21:51,460 --> 00:21:56,819
Seen now, in broad daylight, she looked tall, fair, and shapely.

299
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:03,399
Brown eyes with a benignant light in their irids, and a fine penciling of long lashes

300
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:06,880
round, relieved the whiteness of her large front.

301
00:22:08,180 --> 00:22:13,699
On each of her temples, her hair, of a very dark brown, was clustered in

302
00:22:13,701 --> 00:22:17,539
round curls, according to the fashion of those times.

303
00:22:18,470 --> 00:22:22,880
When neither smooth bands nor long ringlets were invoked, her dress,

304
00:22:23,659 --> 00:22:29,100
also in the mode of the day, was of purple cloth, relieved by a sort of Spanish

305
00:22:29,100 --> 00:22:34,659
trimming of black velvet, a gold watch, watches were not so common then as now,

306
00:22:35,039 --> 00:22:36,140
shone at her girdle.

307
00:22:37,210 --> 00:22:42,619
Let the reader add to complete the picture, refined features, a complexion,

308
00:22:42,880 --> 00:22:49,460
if pale, clear, and a stately air and carriage, and he will have, at least,

309
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:55,820
as clearly as words can give it, a correct idea of the exterior of Miss Temple.

310
00:22:56,289 --> 00:22:59,484
Maria Temple, as I afterwards saw the name written

311
00:22:59,484 --> 00:23:02,960
in a prayer book entrusted to me to carry to church.

312
00:23:04,449 --> 00:23:09,199
The superintendent of Lowwood, for such was this lady, having taken her

313
00:23:09,201 --> 00:23:14,960
seat before a pair of globes placed on one of the tables, summoned the first class

314
00:23:14,961 --> 00:23:18,640
round her, and commenced giving a lesson on geography.

315
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:25,180
The lower classes were called by the teachers, repetitions in history, grammar, etc.

316
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:30,239
, went on for an hour, writing and arithmetic succeeded,

317
00:23:30,975 --> 00:23:34,779
and music lessons were given by Miss Temple to some of the elder girls.

318
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:41,659
The duration of each lesson was measured by the clock, which at last struck twelve.

319
00:23:42,479 --> 00:23:44,220
The super-intend rose.

320
00:23:45,739 --> 00:23:49,079
I have a word to address to the pupils, said she.

321
00:23:50,119 --> 00:23:53,021
The tumult of cessation from lessons was already

322
00:23:53,023 --> 00:23:56,461
breaking forth, but it sank at her voice.

323
00:23:56,699 --> 00:23:57,699
She went on.

324
00:23:59,029 --> 00:24:03,579
You had this morning a breakfast which you could not eat, you must be hungry.

325
00:24:04,460 --> 00:24:09,159
I have ordered that a lunch of bread and cheese shall be served to all.

326
00:24:09,930 --> 00:24:12,579
The teachers looked at her with a sort of surprise.

327
00:24:14,239 --> 00:24:16,359
It is to be done on my responsibility.

328
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:23,739
She added, in an explanatory tone to them, and immediately afterwards left the room.

329
00:24:25,579 --> 00:24:28,929
The bread and cheese was presently brought in and distributed

330
00:24:28,930 --> 00:24:31,979
to the high delight and refreshment of the whole school.

331
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:36,079
The order was now given to the garden.

332
00:24:37,329 --> 00:24:40,715
Each put on a coarse straw bonnet with strings

333
00:24:40,716 --> 00:24:44,201
of coloured calico and a cloak of grey freeze.

334
00:24:45,500 --> 00:24:51,761
I was similarly equipped, and following the stream, I made my way into the open air.

335
00:24:52,689 --> 00:24:56,561
The garden was a wide enclosure, surrounded with

336
00:24:56,563 --> 00:25:00,479
walls so high as to exclude every glimpse of prospect.

337
00:25:01,789 --> 00:25:05,756
A covered veranda ran down one side, and broad walks

338
00:25:05,756 --> 00:25:09,720
bordered a middle space divided into scores of little beds.

339
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:13,297
These beds were assigned as gardens for the

340
00:25:13,298 --> 00:25:16,761
pupils to cultivate, and each bed had an owner.

341
00:25:17,430 --> 00:25:23,640
When full of flowers, they would doubtless look pretty, but now, at the latter end of

342
00:25:23,640 --> 00:25:27,560
January, all was wintry blight and brown decay.

343
00:25:28,675 --> 00:25:31,739
I shuddered as I stood and looked round me.

344
00:25:32,619 --> 00:25:37,359
It was an inclement day for outdoor exercise, not positively rainy,

345
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:40,199
but darkened by a drizzling yellow fog.

346
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:45,140
All underfoot was still soaking wet with the floods of yesterday.

347
00:25:46,770 --> 00:25:52,979
The stronger among the girls ran about and engaged in active games, but sundry pale

348
00:25:52,980 --> 00:25:57,239
and thin ones herded together for shelter and warmth in the veranda.

349
00:25:58,670 --> 00:26:03,659
And amongst these, as the dense mist penetrated to their shivering frames,

350
00:26:04,739 --> 00:26:07,239
I heard frequently the sound of a hollow cough.

351
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:12,760
As yet, I had spoken to no one, nor did anybody seem to take notice of me.

352
00:26:13,340 --> 00:26:14,479
I stood lonely enough.

353
00:26:15,949 --> 00:26:18,819
But to that feeling of isolation, I was accustomed.

354
00:26:19,850 --> 00:26:21,300
It did not oppress me much.

355
00:26:22,564 --> 00:26:27,960
I lent against a pillar of the veranda, drew my gray mantle close about me and

356
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:33,760
trying to forget the cold which nipped me without, and the unsatisfied hunger which

357
00:26:33,761 --> 00:26:39,180
nought me within, delivered myself up to the employment of watching and thinking.

358
00:26:40,539 --> 00:26:44,420
My reflections were too undefined and fragmentary to merit record.

359
00:26:45,649 --> 00:26:47,359
I hardly yet knew where I was.

360
00:26:48,319 --> 00:26:52,680
Gateshead and my past life seemed floated away to an immeasurable distance.

361
00:26:53,609 --> 00:26:59,900
The present was vague and strange, and of the future I could form no conjecture.

362
00:27:01,899 --> 00:27:06,920
I looked around the convent like garden, and then up at the house, a large

363
00:27:06,921 --> 00:27:12,520
building, half of which seemed gray and old, the other half quite new.

364
00:27:13,680 --> 00:27:18,979
The new part containing the school room in dormitory was lit by mulliend and lattice

365
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:23,323
to windows which gave it a church-like aspect, a stone tablet

366
00:27:23,323 --> 00:27:27,300
over the door bore this inscription, lowered institution.

367
00:27:29,420 --> 00:27:36,640
This portion was rebuilt anodomony unknown by Naomi Brocklehurst of Brocklehurst Hall

368
00:27:36,840 --> 00:27:37,840
in this county.

369
00:27:39,010 --> 00:27:43,878
Let your light so shine before men that they may see your

370
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:47,960
good works and glorify your father which is in heaven.

371
00:27:48,939 --> 00:27:50,600
St. Matthew, verse 16.

372
00:27:52,199 --> 00:27:54,079
I read these words over and over again.

373
00:27:54,930 --> 00:27:57,832
I felt that an explanation belonged to them

374
00:27:57,832 --> 00:28:01,121
and was unable fully to penetrate their import.

375
00:28:03,265 --> 00:28:09,720
I was still pondering the signification of institution and endeavouring to make out a

376
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:15,279
connection between the first words and the verse of scripture when the sound of a

377
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:17,640
cough close behind me made me turn my head.

378
00:28:19,569 --> 00:28:21,960
I saw a girl sitting on a stone bench near.

379
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:27,060
She was bent over a book on the perusal of which she seemed intent.

380
00:28:28,079 --> 00:28:30,520
From where I stood, I could see the title.

381
00:28:31,039 --> 00:28:36,960
It was Rassolas, a name that struck me as strange and consequently attractive.

382
00:28:38,145 --> 00:28:44,340
In turning a leaf, she happened to look up and I said to her directly, is your book

383
00:28:44,489 --> 00:28:45,489
interesting?

384
00:28:46,390 --> 00:28:49,739
I had already formed the intention of asking her to lend it to me someday.

385
00:28:51,010 --> 00:28:52,010
I like it.

386
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:58,380
She answered after a pause of a second or two during which she examined me.

387
00:28:59,989 --> 00:29:00,989
What is it about?

388
00:29:01,659 --> 00:29:02,659
I continued.

389
00:29:03,359 --> 00:29:05,444
I hardly know where I found the hardy hood

390
00:29:05,444 --> 00:29:08,480
thus to open a conversation with a stranger.

391
00:29:08,949 --> 00:29:13,085
The step was contrary to my nature and habits, but I think

392
00:29:13,086 --> 00:29:16,199
her occupation touched a chord of sympathy somewhere.

393
00:29:17,039 --> 00:29:23,439
For I too liked reading, though of a frivolous and childish kind, I could not

394
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:26,619
digest or comprehend the serious or substantial.

395
00:29:28,229 --> 00:29:31,520
You may look at it, replied the girl offering me the book.

396
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:33,680
I did so.

397
00:29:34,220 --> 00:29:38,560
A brief examination convinced me that the contents were less taking than the title.

398
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:42,800
Rassolas looked dull to my trifling taste.

399
00:29:43,859 --> 00:29:47,546
I saw nothing about fairies, nothing about genie, no bright

400
00:29:47,547 --> 00:29:50,460
variety seemed spread over the closely printed pages.

401
00:29:51,229 --> 00:29:52,420
I returned it to her.

402
00:29:53,239 --> 00:29:56,145
She received it quietly, and without saying anything

403
00:29:56,146 --> 00:29:59,579
she was about to relapse into her former studious mood.

404
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,819
Again, I ventured to disturb her.

405
00:30:03,930 --> 00:30:07,020
Can you tell me what the writing on that stone over the door means?

406
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:09,420
What is lowwood institution?

407
00:30:10,750 --> 00:30:12,699
This house where you are come to live.

408
00:30:14,130 --> 00:30:16,079
And why do they call it institution?

409
00:30:17,085 --> 00:30:18,979
Is it in any way different from other schools?

410
00:30:20,774 --> 00:30:22,640
It is partly a charity school.

411
00:30:23,119 --> 00:30:26,819
You and I and all the rest of us are charity children.

412
00:30:27,420 --> 00:30:28,880
I suppose you are an orphan.

413
00:30:29,659 --> 00:30:31,979
Are not either your father or your mother dead?

414
00:30:33,369 --> 00:30:35,359
Both died before I can remember.

415
00:30:37,010 --> 00:30:41,153
Well, all the girls here have lost either one or both parents,

416
00:30:41,154 --> 00:30:45,560
and this is called an institution for educating orphans.

417
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:47,779
Do we pay no money?

418
00:30:48,539 --> 00:30:49,659
Do they keep us for nothing?

419
00:30:50,520 --> 00:30:55,159
We pay, or our friends pay, 15 pounds a year for each.

420
00:30:57,289 --> 00:30:59,359
Then why do they call us charity children?

421
00:31:00,869 --> 00:31:04,844
Because 15 pounds is not enough for bored in teaching,

422
00:31:04,845 --> 00:31:07,500
and the deficiency is supplied by subscription.

423
00:31:09,090 --> 00:31:10,090
Who subscribes?

424
00:31:11,164 --> 00:31:17,240
Different benevolent minded ladies and gentlemen in this neighborhood and in London.

425
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:20,420
Who was Naomi Brockelhurst?

426
00:31:22,100 --> 00:31:27,224
The lady who built the new part of this house as

427
00:31:27,225 --> 00:31:31,100
that sun overlooks and directs everything here.

428
00:31:32,380 --> 00:31:33,380
Why?

429
00:31:34,170 --> 00:31:37,380
Because he is treasurer and manager of the establishment.

430
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:42,819
Then this house does not belong to that tall lady who wears

431
00:31:42,820 --> 00:31:45,560
a watch, and who said we were to have some bread and cheese?

432
00:31:47,100 --> 00:31:48,100
To Miss Temple?

433
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:50,840
Oh no, I wish it did.

434
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:52,779
She has to answer to Mr.

435
00:31:59,039 --> 00:32:00,280
Brockelhurst Does he live here?

436
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:03,279
No, two miles off at a large hall.

437
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:04,920
Is he a good man?

438
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:08,899
He is a clergyman and is said to do a great deal of good.

439
00:32:10,069 --> 00:32:12,439
Did you say that tall lady was called Miss Temple?

440
00:32:13,479 --> 00:32:14,479
Yes.

441
00:32:14,939 --> 00:32:16,600
And what are the other teachers called?

442
00:32:17,800 --> 00:32:20,659
The one with red cheeks is called Miss Smith.

443
00:32:27,659 --> 00:32:31,680
She the little one with black hair is misscatchered.

444
00:32:32,359 --> 00:32:38,140
She teaches history and grammar and hears the second-class repetitions and the one

445
00:32:38,140 --> 00:32:40,917
who wears a shawl and has a pocket hankerchief tied

446
00:32:40,918 --> 00:32:45,079
to her side with a yellow ribboned is Madame Pierrot.

447
00:32:46,289 --> 00:32:49,899
She comes from Leal in France and teaches French.

448
00:32:52,069 --> 00:32:53,069
Do you like the teachers?

449
00:32:53,699 --> 00:32:54,699
Well enough.

450
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:57,485
Do you like the little black one and the

451
00:32:57,487 --> 00:33:01,301
Madame I cannot pronounce her name as you do.

452
00:33:02,119 --> 00:33:03,460
Misscatchered is hasty.

453
00:33:04,170 --> 00:33:05,720
You must take care not to offend her.

454
00:33:06,359 --> 00:33:08,619
Madame Pierrot is not a bad sort of person.

455
00:33:10,250 --> 00:33:12,800
But Miss Temple is the best, isn't she?

456
00:33:13,979 --> 00:33:16,520
Miss Temple is very good and very clever.

457
00:33:16,760 --> 00:33:20,359
She is above the rest because she knows far more than they do.

458
00:33:21,260 --> 00:33:22,260
Have you been long here?

459
00:33:23,199 --> 00:33:24,199
Two years.

460
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:25,640
Are you an orphan?

461
00:33:26,329 --> 00:33:27,329
My mother is dead.

462
00:33:28,340 --> 00:33:29,340
Are you happy here?

463
00:33:30,340 --> 00:33:32,159
You ask rather too many questions.

464
00:33:33,060 --> 00:33:34,979
I have given you answers enough for the present.

465
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:36,880
Now I want to read.

466
00:33:38,439 --> 00:33:41,359
But at that moment, the summons sounded for dinner.

467
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:43,699
All re-entered the house.

468
00:33:44,930 --> 00:33:49,539
The odour which now filled the refectory was scarcely more appetizing than that

469
00:33:49,541 --> 00:33:51,659
which had regaled our nostrils at breakfast.

470
00:33:52,829 --> 00:33:56,439
The dinner was served in two huge tin -plated vessels.

471
00:33:57,439 --> 00:34:01,479
Once rose a strong steam red-lint of rancid fat.

472
00:34:02,750 --> 00:34:06,452
I found the mess to consist of indifferent potatoes and

473
00:34:06,453 --> 00:34:10,119
strange shreds of rusty meat mixed and cooked together.

474
00:34:11,260 --> 00:34:16,439
Of this preparation, a tolerably abundant plateful was apportioned to each pupil.

475
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:20,833
I ate what I could and wandered within myself

476
00:34:20,835 --> 00:34:24,240
whether every day's fare would be like this.

477
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:29,943
After dinner, we immediately adjourned to the schoolroom,

478
00:34:29,944 --> 00:34:33,319
lessons recommenced and were continued till five o'clock.

479
00:34:34,529 --> 00:34:39,960
The only marked event of the afternoon was that I saw the girl with whom I had

480
00:34:39,961 --> 00:34:46,539
conversed in the veranda dismissed in disgrace by miscatured from a history

481
00:34:46,541 --> 00:34:51,619
class and sent to stand in the middle of the large schoolroom.

482
00:34:52,390 --> 00:34:55,461
The punishment seemed to me in a high degree

483
00:34:55,462 --> 00:34:58,600
ignominious, especially for so great a girl.

484
00:34:58,779 --> 00:35:00,460
She looked thirteen or upwards.

485
00:35:01,479 --> 00:35:04,659
I expected she would show signs of great distress and shame.

486
00:35:05,739 --> 00:35:09,000
But to my surprise, she neither wept nor blushed.

487
00:35:09,385 --> 00:35:11,960
Composed, though grave, she stood.

488
00:35:12,550 --> 00:35:14,319
The central mark of all eyes.

489
00:35:15,699 --> 00:35:20,359
How can she bear it so quietly, so firmly, I asked of myself?

490
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:23,939
Where I in her place, it seems to me I should

491
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:27,121
wish the earth to open and swallow me up.

492
00:35:27,420 --> 00:35:30,399
She looks as if she were thinking of something beyond her punishment,

493
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:37,779
beyond her situation, of something not round her nor before her.

494
00:35:39,899 --> 00:35:41,500
I have heard of daydreams.

495
00:35:41,979 --> 00:35:43,180
Is she in a daydream now?

496
00:35:44,260 --> 00:35:47,439
Her eyes are fixed on the floor, but I am sure they do not see it.

497
00:35:48,250 --> 00:35:51,819
Her sight seems turned in, gone down into her heart.

498
00:35:52,939 --> 00:35:57,920
She is looking at what she can remember, I believe, not at what is really present.

499
00:35:58,750 --> 00:36:01,880
I wonder what sort of a girl she is, whether good or naughty.

500
00:36:04,619 --> 00:36:08,722
Soon after 5 pm, we had another meal, consisting of a

501
00:36:08,724 --> 00:36:11,920
small mug of coffee and half a slice of brown bread.

502
00:36:12,870 --> 00:36:16,120
I devoured my bread and drank my coffee with relish.

503
00:36:16,879 --> 00:36:19,020
But I should have been glad of as much more.

504
00:36:19,860 --> 00:36:21,159
I was still hungry.

505
00:36:22,309 --> 00:36:24,200
Half an hour's recreation succeeded.

506
00:36:24,899 --> 00:36:25,899
Then study.

507
00:36:26,459 --> 00:36:30,600
Then the glass of water and the piece of oat cake, prayers and bed.

508
00:36:31,489 --> 00:36:33,719
Such was my first day at Lowwood.
